          BEFORE THE NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION

IN THE MATTER OF THE APPLICATION
OF EL PASO ELECTRIC COMPANY FOR
REVISION OF ITS RETAIL ELECTRIC                             Case No. 25-00082-UT
RATES PURSUANT TO ADVICE NOTICE
NO. 317



EL PASO ELECTRIC COMPANY AND NEW MEXICO STATE UNIVERSITY’S JOINT
STIPULATED RESOLUTION TO NMSU’S NOTICE OF INTENT TO USE MATERIAL
                   DESIGNATED AS CONFIDENTIAL

         El Paso Electric Company (“EPE”), together with the Regents of New Mexico State

University (“NMSU”), hereby notify the Hearing Examiners that counsel for EPE and NMSU have

conferred and have reached the following stipulated resolution of NMSU’s Notice of Intent to Use

Material Designated as Confidential (filed Oct. 23, 2026) in lieu of filing an objection to public

disclosure and request for ruling on confidentiality pursuant to Paragraph L of the Protective

Order:


         1.    EPE waives its confidentiality claims to the excerpts designated as confidential

material on page 22 lines 1-13 and lines 15-34 of the Confidential Direct Testimony and Exhibits

of Michael P. Gorman filed October 23, 2026; and

         2.    EPE waives its confidentiality claims to the excerpts designated as confidential

material on page 25 in Table 5 of the Confidential Direct Testimony and Exhibits of Michael P.

Gorman filed October 23, 2026; and

         3.    EPE waives its confidentiality claims to the excerpts designated as confidential

material on page 27 lines 3-8 of the Confidential Direct Testimony and Exhibits of Michael P.

Gorman filed October 23, 2026.
           4.   EPE stipulates that excerpted material on the foregoing pages in the Confidential

Direct Testimony of Michael P. Gorman accurately states Confidential Information that EPE

provided through discovery in this case, and EPE will not object to admission of those statements

into the record for this proceeding on the basis of foundation or authenticity.

          5.   Given these stipulations, NMSU no longer intends to use the additional confidential

material designated as Confidential Exhibit MPG-21 in pre-filed testimony or at the hearing in this

matter.

          6.   Accordingly, EPE and NMSU agree that upon filing of this Stipulation, NMSU will

file a motion to withdraw the confidential version of Michael P. Gorman’s direct testimony

including Confidential Exhibit MPG-21 and file a replacement unredacted version of the Public

Direct Testimony and Exhibits of Michael P. Gorman.



